# Pulse CRM — Environment Contract
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values for your environment.
# `.env` is gitignored; never commit real credentials.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL (required)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL connection string used by Prisma (both the CLI via
# prisma.config.ts and the runtime client in lib/prisma.ts via @prisma/adapter-pg).
# Format: postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE
#
# Local development uses a Docker Postgres container published on host port 5433
# (see docs/decisions.md, ADR-020). Point production at your managed database.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5433/pulse_crm"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NODE_ENV (do not set manually)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by lib/prisma.ts to decide whether to cache the Prisma client across
# hot reloads. It is set automatically by Next.js / Node ("development",
# "production", "test"), so you normally do NOT define it here.
